**** Installing AdGaurd on Proxmox ****

1. In the Server Hosting Proxmox
  a. CT ID: xxx
  b. Hostname: adguard
  c. Password: uptoyou
  d. Template: Ubuntu
  e. Disk: 4GB
  f. CPU: 1 core
  g. RAM: 256MB
  h. IP/CIDR: 192.168.1.x/24
  i. Gateway: 192.168.1.1

2. In the Server shell
  run: nano /etc/pve/lxc/xxx.conf
  add: unprivileged: 0
       features: nesting=1,keyctl=1

3. Start and enter the container
  a. pct start xxx
  b. pct enter xxx

4. Setting up the network
  a. ip addr add 192.168.1.x/24 dev eth0
  b. ip link set eth0 up
  c. ip route add default via 192.168.1.1
  d. nano /etc/network/interfaces
    e.  auto lo
        iface lo inet loopback

        auto eth0
        iface eth0 inet static
              address 192.168.1.x/24
              gateway 192.168.1.1
              dns-nameservers 8.8.8.8

5. Now you have internet
  a. apt update && apt upgrade -y
  b. apt install curl wget -y

6. Install AdGuard
  a. wget -O /tmp/adguard.tar.gz https://static.adtidy.org/adguardhome/release/AdGuardHome_linux_amd64.tar.gz
  b. tar -xvzf /tmp/adguard.tar.gz -C /tmp
  c. mv /tmp/AdGuardHome/AdGuardHome /usr/local/bin/
  d. AdGuardHome -s install

7. Install and start it
  a. AdGuardHome -s install
  b. AdGuardHome -s start

8. Set it up on the browser
  a. http://192.168.1.x:3000
  b. Admin interface port: 3000
  c. DNS Server Port: 53
  d. Username and password as you wish

9. Enable auto start
  Click on the container > Optoins > Start to boot >> Yes
